your booth or later?

00:48:07.500 --> 00:48:11.580
STEPHANE DONZE: Yeah, so the key
things, and I kind of touched

00:48:11.580 --> 00:48:17.040
that in the beginning, is we are
combining all of the features

00:48:17.040 --> 00:48:18.690
that Rosemary was talking about.

00:48:18.690 --> 00:48:20.970
We are replacing
sharp point, replacing

00:48:20.970 --> 00:48:23.550
all of those old systems
with the same feature level,

00:48:23.550 --> 00:48:27.210
and sometimes even superior
feature levels, but in a way

00:48:27.210 --> 00:48:30.210
that respects the Google
user experience that

00:48:30.210 --> 00:48:31.610
makes it easy for the end user.

00:48:31.610 --> 00:48:33.930
So the feedback we get
from all of our customers,

00:48:33.930 --> 00:48:36.180
oh my god, this is so much
easier than [INAUDIBLE],

00:48:36.180 --> 00:48:37.846
this is so much easier
than Lotus Notes,

00:48:37.846 --> 00:48:40.770
it's so much easier than Open
Text, and so on and so forth.

00:48:40.770 --> 00:48:44.870
We bring those systems to
the Google environment,

00:48:44.870 --> 00:48:47.130
to the Google user
experience, and it gets them

00:48:47.130 --> 00:48:48.690
to be so much more productive.

00:48:48.690 --> 00:48:50.820
So it's really our
integration with the G Suite,

00:48:50.820 --> 00:48:53.880
our embracement
of the simplicity,

00:48:53.880 --> 00:48:56.220
the flexibility, the
collaboration aspects of the G

00:48:56.220 --> 00:48:56.820
Suite.

00:48:56.820 --> 00:49:00.510
And even more than that, we
have built an operating system.

00:49:00.510 --> 00:49:04.440
So we think of AODocs not
just as a box in which you can

00:49:04.440 --> 00:49:06.210
put documents, it's a platform.

00:49:06.210 --> 00:49:08.310
So it's integrated with
G Suite, obviously,

00:49:08.310 --> 00:49:10.830
but it's also integrated with
the rest of the ecosystem.

00:49:10.830 --> 00:49:14.600
We work with Docusign, we can
have a document in AODocs,

00:49:14.600 --> 00:49:16.800
send it to Docusign,
get it back signed.

00:49:16.800 --> 00:49:19.890
We work with virtual, we can
have the virtual encryption

00:49:19.890 --> 00:49:22.560
engine that was
described by Charles,

00:49:22.560 --> 00:49:24.870
and apply to AODocs
content, and have

00:49:24.870 --> 00:49:27.930
AODocs enforce the
encryption for you

00:49:27.930 --> 00:49:31.720
so that you get the compliance
levels that you need to have.

00:49:31.720 --> 00:49:34.830
And even getting further, all
