like RingCentral?

00:50:42.120 --> 00:50:43.950
MACK KHORRAMI: So
we're a global company.

00:50:43.950 --> 00:50:48.180
Our products are sold in more
than 100 countries globally.

00:50:48.180 --> 00:50:51.840
We have 600 retail
stores globally,

00:50:51.840 --> 00:50:57.400
with 300 in US and Canada,
and rest in EMEA and APAC.

00:50:57.400 --> 00:51:03.710
A few years ago we started
working on our Omni channel.

00:51:03.710 --> 00:51:05.670
To implement the
correct Omni channel,

00:51:05.670 --> 00:51:14.250
you needed a very nice
steady, stable infrastructure.

00:51:14.250 --> 00:51:18.240
To do that, at that time
our retailer stores had

00:51:18.240 --> 00:51:21.780
only three POTS
lines with no IVR

00:51:21.780 --> 00:51:24.750
capability, no good functions.

00:51:24.750 --> 00:51:27.090
So we started looking,
we talked to Cisco,

00:51:27.090 --> 00:51:31.170
we talked to Avaya back then,
but the price was really

00:51:31.170 --> 00:51:32.730
out of our range.

00:51:32.730 --> 00:51:41.200
What we did, we went
ahead and talked to AT&amp;T,

00:51:41.200 --> 00:51:46.150
and AT&amp;T came to us
and said, hey, we

00:51:46.150 --> 00:51:49.000
have this product that we
think you're going to like.

00:51:49.000 --> 00:51:52.600
It's in your price range, and
one of the local retailers

00:51:52.600 --> 00:51:55.310
in Dallas area uses it as well.

00:51:55.310 --> 00:51:57.750
So that's how the
journey started.

00:51:57.750 --> 00:51:59.310
THORSTEN LUEDECKE: Excellent.

00:51:59.310 --> 00:52:01.805
ERIC BOHREN: And Mack,
you adopted communications

00:52:01.805 --> 00:52:03.930
