right move to make?

00:52:17.730 --> 00:52:20.150
MACK KHORRAMI: So
I'm old Telco guy,

00:52:20.150 --> 00:52:21.730
I used to work for a carrier.

00:52:21.730 --> 00:52:28.500
So I knew how hard it is for
partners to get certified.

00:52:28.500 --> 00:52:33.620
So one of the major selling
points to my customers

00:52:33.620 --> 00:52:38.250
and to our customers was that
AT&amp;T has certified RingCentral.

00:52:38.250 --> 00:52:44.730
And another one, we discussed
it with the local retailer,

00:52:44.730 --> 00:52:47.500
we discussed to see how
they're comfortable with it.

00:52:47.500 --> 00:52:51.610
And I promised our
internal customers

00:52:51.610 --> 00:52:56.340
that we will have a solid
plan, we will test everything

00:52:56.340 --> 00:52:59.250
in our lab, and we
will not implement it

00:52:59.250 --> 00:53:03.752
without they actually
see it for themselves.

00:53:03.752 --> 00:53:04.960
THORSTEN LUEDECKE: Excellent.

00:53:04.960 --> 00:53:06.720
ERIC BOHREN: And
so Mack, what use

00:53:06.720 --> 00:53:12.310
cases were critical to
your evaluation for FOSSIL?

00:53:12.310 --> 00:53:13.930
MACK KHORRAMI: IVR
was number one.

00:53:13.930 --> 00:53:19.010
Basically productivity
was very important to us.

00:53:21.820 --> 00:53:25.240
We don't want our
retail employees

00:53:25.240 --> 00:53:28.030
to waste their time on phone.

00:53:28.030 --> 00:53:33.260
So if they were
assisting a customer,

00:53:33.260 --> 00:53:38.780
and they would get a call,
the caller could actually

00:53:38.780 --> 00:53:41.990
select the button,
and they would

00:53:41.990 --> 00:53:45.050
talk to somebody like with
our Richardson office.

00:53:45.050 --> 00:53:48.950
In addition, we enabled
eight digit dialing.

00:53:48.950 --> 00:53:54.957
So in New York we have
five stores right next

00:53:54.957 --> 00:53:55.540
to each other.

00:53:55.540 --> 00:53:57.110
So if they wanted
to help a customer,

00:53:57.110 --> 00:54:05.180
instead of calling the store
by the old MPA and execs,

00:54:05.180 --> 00:54:08.390
they could just use the
stored number and call them.

00:54:08.390 --> 00:54:09.620
So that was very nice.

00:54:09.620 --> 00:54:11.360
And also they could
call corporate,

00:54:11.360 --> 00:54:14.190
and corporate can call eight
digit dialing by just the store

00:54:14.190 --> 00:54:15.072
numbers.

00:54:15.072 --> 00:54:16.280
THORSTEN LUEDECKE: Excellent.

00:54:16.280 --> 00:54:16.779
Thank you.

